<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

<!--
    Infestation_PlanetwideBan.xml                                Jawa_Patches
    ============================================================================
    SANDBUSTER_CASTES_BUILD_1 — dune_sea.md's "Amendment — the sand busters"
    (owner-ruled 2026-09-24, NIGHTSIDE_ICE_DESIGN_SITTING_1): "the event is
    banned everywhere else on the planet as part of the Utinni scenario —
    the campaign layer suppresses the incident planet-wide, and only the
    Dune Sea carries it."

    Vanilla Core's own IncidentDef defName="Infestation" is zeroed out
    EVERYWHERE, Stillsand included — not narrowed with disallowedBiomes to
    exclude just the Dune Sea, because the Dune Sea does not get vanilla
    Infestation either: it gets the re-skinned RM_SandBusterEruption
    (mandrake.rm.stillsand, RM_SandBusterEruption.xml), which confines
    itself to RM_Stillsand via its own <allowedBiomes> field. So this
    incident's correct footprint is the empty set on every biome, which a
    flat baseChance=0 gives directly — an allowedBiomes/disallowedBiomes
    pair would have to enumerate every OTHER biome (or use disallowedBiomes
    with RM_Stillsand on it, which would wrongly leave the incident live
    there instead of the sand-buster replacement). baseChance=0 is also this
    repo's own established pattern for "the mod stays active, the incident
    just never fires again" — same mechanism as
    MoEventsChancesZeroed_RuledCut.xml (MODLIST_RULED_CUTS_1), reused here
    against a Core def instead of a third-party mod's.

    baseChanceWithRoyalty is left untouched: the live IncidentDef dump
    (RimSage, 2026-09-27) carries no override for it (default -1), so
    ModsConfig.RoyaltyActive never reads it in preference to baseChance —
    zeroing baseChance alone is sufficient regardless of which DLCs are
    active (and per CLAUDE.md, every DLC is assumed active anyway).

    Scope, deliberately narrow: this patch touches ONLY the storyteller-
    picked IncidentDef defName="Infestation" (RimWorld.
    IncidentWorker_Infestation) — the classic bug-storm event the amendment
    names ("vanilla's infestation event — the huge insects that burst from
    the ground"). It does NOT touch DeepDrillInfestation (a different
    incident, triggered by the player's own deep-drilling action rather than
    the storyteller), WastepackInfestation, Infestation_Jelly, or Anomaly's
    own ComplexThreatDef defName="Infestation" (a different def type/system
    entirely) — none of those are the incident the amendment describes, and
    banning them was never asked for. If a future ruling widens the ban to
    those, it is separate work, not an omission here.

    No PatchOperationFindMod guard: this targets a Core IncidentDef, which
    is always present regardless of the active mod list (unlike
    MoEventsChancesZeroed_RuledCut.xml's third-party-mod target).
-->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/IncidentDef[defName="Infestation"]/baseChance</xpath>
    <value>
      <baseChance>0</baseChance>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
